{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'find .codex/skills -maxdepth 4 -type f; ls -R source_evidence | head -90; cat .agentic_paper_workspace.json; cat paper_strategy.json | head -100; cat .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh | head -65; ls /usr/local/bin | head; command -v pdflatex; command -v apply_patch; cat references_provenance.json | head -60'","aggregated_output":".codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.bst\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/references.bib\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/alifeconf.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/s2_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/scholarly_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/openalex_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\nsource_evidence:\ndownstream\n\nsource_evidence/downstream:\nbaseline\nprogram\n\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline:\nprogram_spec.toml\nsrc\n\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/src:\nprogram.py\n\nsource_evidence/downstream/program:\nprogram_spec.toml\nsrc\n\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/src:\nIMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md\nprogram.py\n{\n  \"global_memory_dir\": \"work/results/t03/codex/20261117_144926/investigation\",\n  \"output_dir\": \"work/results/t03/codex/20261117_144926/paper\",\n  \"results_dir\": \"work/results/t03/codex/20261117_144926/investigation\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"task_dir\": \"work/results/t03/codex/20261117_144926/task\"\n}\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"Repeatability and Reference Fidelity of Finite-Budget SHAP\",\n  \"central_question\": \"For fixed trained tabular models and empirical interventional games, how do finite-budget SHAP estimates compare in repeat agreement, reference fidelity, and measured cost, and does averaging four short runs help relative to one longer run at equal coalition count?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"In the retained two-dataset audit, repeat agreement and near-exact additivity do not certify reference fidelity, and averaging four short explanations has lower mean reference fidelity than one longer explanation at equal coalition count; neither observation establishes universal unreliability or sampler superiority.\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"A standalone empirical audit is supported by retained attributions, references, measured costs, within-fit input-cluster intervals, and a completed final evaluation. The strongest result is a calibrated distinction between repeated top-feature agreement, reference-sensitive attribution error, and budget allocation, not a winning optimization method. German Credit and California ACSIncome share one empirical interventional estimand but require separate reference-quality evidence blocks: approximate references for German Credit and exact coalition references for ACSIncome. The frozen studied sampler was selected without a qualifying search winner. Independent final qualification is completed/qualified/true, not failed. Descriptive final metrics and unverified retained diagnostics do not establish generalization, causal validity, or deployment safety.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"recentered\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not an edit-mode preservation decision: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, or extra_tasks inputs are present. Recenter the broad source-task ambition and speculative memory on the actual frozen sampler and retained audit. A prior manuscript is not claimed to exist. Reject a winning-sampler story; reject a universal high-risk deployment verdict; prefer the shared fixed-game audit with reference-specific evidence blocks. An available detailed implementation is not evidence of superiority.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"Direct inspection of source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py identifies stratified kernel-size sampling, complement-pair coverage, rank headroom, and the unchanged efficiency-constrained least-squares solver; this is the studied method, not the later conditioning or interaction-alias proposals.\",\n    \"Direct inspection of source_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py identifies independent kernel-marginal sampling with the same solver. Its original search comparison is retained as context; no paired final attribution arrays for this original sampler were found.\",\n    \"study.* identifies a non-winner selection, three scored attempts, zero unscored attempts, and zero search-score difference from the original baseline. These selection facts cannot substitute for final scientific comparisons.\",\n    \"final.qualification.* independently reports completed, qualified, and true. Do not invent failed qualification from the no-winner search outcome. Missing detailed qualification-gate diagnostics remain unknown.\",\n    \"final.evidence.episodes supplies two fitted seeds, six dataset/model conditions, two backgrounds, two coalition budgets, repeated candidate estimates, package Kernel SHAP comparators, references, and one deterministic replay. Its diagnostics are explicitly unverified; all substantive results must retain this provenance limitation.\",\n    \"The downstream source mapping identifies the staged selected family directly, while its tree digest and the final-evaluation program-tree digest differ. Describe the final linkage as manifest-bound evaluation plus family-level source correspondence, not independently verified exact-file identity; do not discard evaluated family evidence solely because hashes differ.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Stratified complementary coalition sampling\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Frozen studied configuration. Explain kernel-size stratification, complement-pair finite-population coverage, rank headroom, and the fixed constrained solver; proposed labels its role, not demonstrated superiority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Library Kernel SHAP at deployment budgets\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Retained final attribution vectors and prediction-row/CPU counters permit a direct descriptive reference-fidelity comparison at each nominal coalition budget. It is not the original independent sampler and has only one stored call per cell/budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Four-short-run attribution average\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Observed allocation comparator: average four additional 64-coalition explanations and compare with the first 256-coalition explanation from the same fixed game. This is not a clean sampler-component ablation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Exact and high-budget attribution references\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Exact enumeration anchors the ten-player ACSIncome games; two high-budget library references characterize German Credit reference sensitivity. These are accuracy anchors, not competing deployment methods.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Original independent kernel-marginal sampler\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Preserve the original comparator and unchanged-solver relationship. Only search-scope score context is available for its comparison with the frozen method; omit any unmeasured final fidelity or repeatability comparison.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Primary: show repeat top-three-set overlap and reference-fidelity quality separately by dataset, model family, and fitted seed, using existing within-fit input-cluster intervals. Their scales have different meanings; never subtract them or interpret overlap as a probability of a correct explanation.\",\n    \"Primary: report the observed averaging-minus-one-long-run quality difference, with its signed zero reference and stored within-fit intervals. The final mean is -0.03883354541895445; it is not a candidate-minus-original-baseline improvement.\",\n    \"Direct descriptive comparison: frozen sampler versus library Kernel SHAP reference fidelity at nominal budgets 64 and 256, separating both fits and datasets. Check actual prediction rows and distinguish wall durations from package CPU counters.\",\n    \"Condition specificity: distinguish the exact ACSIncome reference setting from approximate German Credit references. Dataset differences are confounded with dimension, data composition, reference construction, and fitted models, not an isolated mechanism.\",\n    \"Report numerical efficiency residuals and evaluator-reported control/completion outcomes as checks, not attribution accuracy, causal validity, or high-risk deployment certification.\",\n    \"Keep search selection and final findings separate. Use study.* for attempt counts and score differences; never turn missing attempts into losses. Omit conditioning/alias branches from core results because there are no controlled final component ablations.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Early full-text-width fixed-game overview connecting repeated estimates, deployment comparator, reference anchors, and equal-coalition-count allocation.\",\n    \"Four-panel agreement/reference-fidelity point-and-interval comparison across model families, with separate rows for the two datasets and separate fitted-seed markers.\",\n    \"Two-panel signed allocation contrast: quality of four-short-run average minus quality of one longer explanation, using stored input-cluster intervals.\",\n    \"Four-panel direct reference-fidelity comparison of studied and library estimators at the two nominal budgets, separating dataset and fitted seed; deterministic summaries from retained vectors only.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"fixed_game_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Make the fixed empirical game, compared estimators, exact versus approximate anchors, and allocation contrast legible at a glance without implying sampler superiority.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"evidence_role\",\n      \"metric\": \"none; conceptual structure only\",\n      \"split_by\": \"reference_kind\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"paper.sty sets a single 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height. Use the full 5.5-inch text width, approximately 1.8-2.0 inches high plus caption, near page 2. A half-text-width diagram would make six semantic groups and reference annotations unreadable.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 1,\n      \"max_panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 4,\n      \"intended_placement\": \"page 1 or 2, preferably page 2 after the research question\",\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 9,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"content_spec\": \"At most six semantic groups: fixed model/input/background and probability estimand; coalition sampling; repeated attributions and library comparator; agreement and fidelity readouts; exact ACSIncome/two approximate German references; four short versus one long allocation. Mark evidence scope and unverified diagnostics in the caption. Arrows denote data dependencies, not discovery order or a production certification pipeline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"agreement_and_reference_fidelity\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Contrast repeatability with reference-sensitive quality without conflating metrics or datasets.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"point_interval\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"group_by\": \"model_family\",\n      \"metric\": \"top-three-set overlap and normalized L1 reference-fidelity quality in separate panels\",\n      \"split_by\": \"dataset and metric\",\n      \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n      \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"layout_rationale\": \"At the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width, a 2-by-2 layout gives roughly 2.5 inches per panel, sufficient for three short model labels and two fitted-seed markers. Allocate roughly 2.8 inches plus caption on pages 5-6; use at least 8.5-point final labels and never shrink to half text width.\",\n      \"allow_progression\": false,\n      \"max_panels\": 4,\n      \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n      \"max_series_per_panel\": 2,\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scientific_evidence.py\" \"$@\"\n2to3\n2to3-3.12\nautoillustrate\nclaude\ncodex\ndocutils\ndotenv\ndrawio\ngemini\nheadless\n/usr/bin/pdflatex\n{\n  \"campaign_results_dir\": \"work/results/t03/codex/20261117_144926/investigation\",\n  \"count\": 25,\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-17T17:12:41.822819+00:00\",\n  \"queries\": [\n    \"\\\"A Unified Approach to Interpreting Model Predictions\\\" Lundberg Lee\",\n    \"Shapley value estimation stratified sampling antithetic sampling\",\n    \"\\\"Provably Accurate Shapley Value Estimation via Leverage Score Sampling\\\" Musco Witter\",\n    \"\\\"True to the Model or True to the Data?\\\" Chen Janizek Lundberg Lee\",\n    \"\\\"On the Stability of Feature Selection Algorithms\\\" Nogueira Sechidis Brown\",\n    \"\\\"An empirical study of the effect of background data size on the stability of SHapley Additive exPlanations\\\" Yuan\",\n    \"Shapley value estimation Monte Carlo error confidence intervals\",\n    \"\\\"Retiring Adult: New Datasets for Fair Machine Learning\\\" Ding Hardt Miller Schmidt\",\n    \"\\\"Statlog (German Credit Data)\\\" \\\"10.24432/C5NC77\\\"\"\n  ],\n  \"reference_query_plan\": {\n    \"architectural_shifts\": [],\n    \"benchmarks\": [\n      \"UCI Statlog (German Credit Data), twenty original feature groups; logistic regression, random forest, and gradient boosting\",\n      \"folktables ACSIncome from California 2024 one-year ACS PUMS, ten original feature groups; logistic regression, random forest, and gradient boosting\",\n      \"Synthetic constant, copied-feature and feature-permutation controls; validation controls rather than additional public benchmarks\"\n    ],\n    \"central_topic\": \"Finite-budget repeat-run reliability of grouped interventional Kernel SHAP for fixed tabular classifiers, distinguishing attribution agreement from reference fidelity and comparing four short explanations with one longer explanation.\",\n    \"comparators\": [\n      \"Independent Shapley-kernel size/subset sampling with the same endpoint-constrained regression, as implemented by the copied baseline\",\n      \"Package KernelExplainer at deployment budgets and at higher reference budgets; not interchangeable with the copied independent-sampling baseline\",\n      \"Stratified and antithetic Monte Carlo Shapley estimation as the methodological comparator for complementary coalition sampling\",\n      \"Leverage-score Shapley estimation and finite-sample accuracy guarantees as literature comparators, not implemented baselines\",\n      \"Chance-corrected feature-selection stability as a conceptual comparator for raw top-three overlap, not a metric implemented in the run\",\n      \"Interventional versus conditional Shapley estimands and background-size sensitivity as semantic context, not experimentally compared estimands\"\n    ],\n    \"core_methods\": [\n      \"Shapley-kernel coalition sampling with endpoint-constrained least-squares attribution on the positive-class probability scale\",\n      \"Randomized size stratification, complementary coalition pairing with rank headroom, and finite-population coverage within complement strata\",\n      \"Exploratory outcome-blind eight-design portfolios selected by contrast rank and inverse-spectrum conditioning or pairwise/three-way interaction alias energy; search-stage alternatives only\",\n      \"Exact coalition-enumeration Shapley references for ten-feature ACSIncome and two independently seeded high-budget KernelExplainer references for twenty-feature German Credit\",\n      \"Top-three absolute-attribution overlap, rank and sign agreement, normalized L1 reference discrepancy, local-accuracy residuals, and explained-input-cluster bootstrap intervals\",\n      \"Equal-coalition-budget comparison of averaging four 64-coalition explanations against one 256-coalition explanation\"\n    ],\n    \"forbidden_query_patterns\": [\n      \"Any attempt to infer, identify, retrieve, access, or use the prohibited prior paper, its title, authors, results, mirrors, preprints, abstract pages, proceedings/review pages, slides, posters, videos, blogs, or code.\",\n      \"Citation-graph expansion, cited-by/related-paper recommendations, reviews, notes, aggregators, social discussions, or reproductions that cite or discuss the prohibited work; do not use starter papers as snowballing entry points.\",\n      \"Broad searches phrased as the task itself, such as SHAP repeated-run reliability tabular models or single-run SHAP reliability, which risk identifying the prohibited study.\",\n      \"Unrestricted exploratory retrieval for the two method-level queries without a safe-source gate; if potentially prohibited content appears, stop reading immediately and record the location, content encountered, and extent read.\",\n      \"FT-Transformer, ResNet, deep tabular architecture transitions, neural-to-tree transfer, TreeSHAP speedups, or cross-architecture superiority claims: none is tested here. The named Yuan study is permitted context, not evidence of a neural experiment.\",\n      \"Pima, Give Me Some Credit, Arrhythmia, or other unexecuted dataset benchmarks; ACS interstate/year transfer or fairness-performance studies not present in the run.\",\n      \"Generic optimization, generic benchmarking, scientific method, paper writing, campaign chronology, milestone searches, or positive-result searches premised on a winning sampler.\",\n      \"Predictive multiplicity across retrained models, causal SHAP validation, adaptive stopping certificates, conditional SHAP experiments, or implemented leverage-score baselines not supported by these artifacts.\"\n    ],\n    \"queries\": [\n      {\n        \"category\": \"core_method\",\n        \"query\": \"\\\"A Unified Approach to Interpreting Model Predictions\\\" Lundberg Lee\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Allowed starter source for additive SHAP, the Shapley kernel, and endpoint efficiency. Copied candidate and baseline sources both retain constrained sampled regression; efficiency must not be presented as proof of reference fidelity.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"category\": \"core_method\",\n        \"query\": \"Shapley value estimation stratified sampling antithetic sampling\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The selected source stratifies coalition sizes, pairs complementary subsets with rank headroom, and covers complement strata before reuse. Search the specific variance-reduction families, without asserting unbiased regression coefficients or measured superiority.\"\n      },\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
