.00638692175980368, -0.023578767186324442, 0.0025274714185996097, -0.030395290662438817, 0.0027921026482436747, -0.003239459829204817, -0.01767854212654381, 0.014215572048000544, 0.006498621240171289], 'matched_average_duration_seconds': [0.015517658088356256, 0.02494458097498864, 0.01990526099689305, 0.017007532995194197], 'metrics': {'local_accuracy_quality': 1.0, 'matched_budget_gain': -0.12159678021836295, 'reference_fidelity': 0.8862078189911089, 'reference_resolution_quality': 0.9920792174602959, 'repeat_agreement': 0.9444444444444444}, 'reference_counts': [{'coalitions': 2048, 'cpu_seconds': 0.10688883900000024, 'prediction_rows': 16377}, {'coalitions': 2048, 'cpu_seco\nFIGS [('fixed_game_overview', 'At most six semantic groups: fixed model/input/background and probability estimand; coalition sampling; repeated attributions and library comparator; agreement and fidelity readouts; exact ACSIncome/two approximate German references; four short versus one long allocation. Mark evidence scope and unverified diagnostics in the caption. Arrows denote data dependencies, not discovery order or a production certification pipeline.'), ('agreement_and_reference_fidelity', 'Rows: German Credit/ACSIncome; columns: repeat overlap/reference fidelity. Show two fits individually. Use case means and stored input_cluster_intervals, both pooled over the same background/budget levels. Caption labels intervals descriptive within-fit 95% input-cluster bootstrap intervals; do not attach pooled intervals to budget-specific points. Explain that exact and approximate fidelity anchors differ.'), ('budget_allocation_contrast', 'Show both fitted seeds separately with stored gain intervals and one common signed interpretation. German gain uses the mean reference vector, whereas its ordinary fidelity metric averages qualities to each reference. Equal coalition count also yields equal candidate oracle masked-row count for a fixed background; it does not imply equal runtime. No significance stars or universal loss claim.'), ('deployment_estimator_comparison', 'Four series: studied-64, studied-256, library-64, library-256. Average within retained input/background cells and candidate repeats, preserving the two fitted seeds in separate panels. Package calls have no estimated seed-to-seed variance. Reconstruct only deterministic summaries from stored vectors, verify candidate reductions against existing summaries, and record formulas and sources. Plot no fabricated error bars. Do not identify the library implementation with the original independent sampler; nominal coalition budgets need not imply identical prediction-row costs.')]\nRESULTS ['Primary: show repeat top-three-set overlap and reference-fidelity quality separately by dataset, model family, and fitted seed, using existing within-fit input-cluster intervals. Their scales have different meanings; never subtract them or interpret overlap as a probability of a correct explanation.', 'Primary: report the observed averaging-minus-one-long-run quality difference, with its signed zero reference and stored within-fit intervals. The final mean is -0.03883354541895445; it is not a candidate-minus-original-baseline improvement.', 'Direct descriptive comparison: frozen sampler versus library Kernel SHAP reference fidelity at nominal budgets 64 and 256, separating both fits and datasets. Check actual prediction rows and distinguish wall durations from package CPU counters.', 'Condition specificity: distinguish the exact ACSIncome reference setting from approximate German Credit references. Dataset differences are confounded with dimension, data composition, reference construction, and fitted models, not an isolated mechanism.', 'Report numerical efficiency residuals and evaluator-reported control/completion outcomes as checks, not attribution accuracy, causal validity, or high-risk deployment certification.', 'Keep search selection and final findings separate. Use study.* for attempt counts and score differences; never turn missing attempts into losses. Omit conditioning/alias branches from core results because there are no controlled final component ablations.']\nNOTES ['This is strategy only. Do not create paper.tex or claims_grounding.json or run final-paper validation in this stage. The downstream writer must follow write-paper-standalone, grounding claims to exact registered sources and preserving qualification facts through review, audit, and revision.', 'Evidence ledger: final.metric.repeat_agreement=0.9458719135802469; final.metric.reference_fidelity=0.9289530659189914; final.metric.local_accuracy_quality=0.9999999999999954; final.metric.matched_budget_gain=-0.03883354541895445; final.metric.reference_resolution_quality=0.992225794670848. These are evaluator-defined descriptive qualities, not calibrated probabilities, statistical significance, or evidence of superiority.', 'The final.qualification.status/outcome/correct sources currently read completed/qualified/true. The study sources report no search winner, not failed final qualification. Gate-level diagnostics not supplied remain unknown. If later authoritative qualification changes to not_qualified, explicitly disclose it in main limitations and preserve all reported restrictions; attribute failure to performance, validity, or adaptivity only if evaluator diagnostics identify that cause.', 'Keep final.evidence.episodes candidate_diagnostics_trust=unverified explicit in the main experimental-evidence subsection and main limitations. Arithmetic reconciliation of retained vectors/aggregates is not an independent execution audit, gate explanation, or source-identity verification. The final scalar aggregates reconcile with six non-replay dataset/model cases per fit.', 'Study scope is German Credit with 20 original players and California 2024 ACSIncome with 10, logistic regression/random forest/gradient boosting, background sizes 8/32, nominal coalition budgets 64/256, six candidate repeats per cell, twelve explained inputs per fit/model, and fitted seeds 7301/9109. Protocol details are grounded in retained episodes plus local evaluator/manifest; do not substitute optional task-brief datasets, neural architectures, or unperformed background-resampling/training-uncertainty studies.', 'Define v_x,B(S) as mean positive-class probability under replacing absent original columns with fixed background rows. Keep the fitted model, explained input, and background fixed within a repeat comparison. Background sizes define different empirical games, not pure Monte Carlo replicas of one estimand. Neither exact enumeration of this game nor agreement with it establishes causal or conditional-expectation faithfulness.', 'Quality is 1/(1+L1(phi-reference)/max(1e-8,L1(reference))). Ordinary German fidelity averages quality against each of two high-budget references; German allocation gain uses their mean vector. ACSIncome uses exact coalition references. Reference agreement alone cannot certify convergence or expose shared reference bias. Near-zero reference norms and magnitude ties constrain interpretation.', 'The paired allocation contrast uses four additional low-budget runs and the first retained high-budget run, not whichever long run looks best and not the first four repeat vectors. It matches coalition counts and, for this candidate oracle at fixed background size, masked prediction rows; repeated endpoints and multi-call overhead still matter. Candidate durations are wall-clock observations; package counters are CPU seconds. Do not compare these clocks as identical.', 'Use existing case-level input-cluster intervals for pooled comparisons. Never treat repeat pairs or multiple backgrounds of one input as independent samples; never combine two fits into a population-level confidence claim. Any new budget-specific interval or statistical test would be a new analysis, not a stored result, and is not required by this strategy. Do not invent acceptability thresholds for single-run explanations.', 'Exclude the terminal deterministic replay from scientific sample sizes and means; retain it only for reproducibility/control reporting. The initial-seed episode includes that replay, while the other fitted-seed episode does not. Synthetic constant/copy/permutation and reset/replay checks are coarse functional checks, not a comprehensive validity or safety audit.', 'Main Table 1: experimental scope, fitted-model families, fixed-game definition, repeats, references, budget units, and seed handling. Main Table 2: measured work by method/budget/background with exact denominators and separated clocks; use existing counters and mark unavailable cells rather than estimating them. Neither table may claim the estimated 24 CPU-hour allowance was measured consumption.', 'Target an 8.7-page body within the VENUE.md 8-9-page requirement: abstract/introduction 1.15; related work 0.65; estimand/design 1.30; sampling/allocation 1.15; metrics/references/uncertainty 1.05; results 2.30; discussion/limitations 0.85; conclusion 0.25. These allocations include figures, captions, and tables, not additional pages. If an 8-page body is used, its last page must be at least 75% full. Use space for estimand clarity, reference limitations, cost comparisons and source caveats, never narrative padding.', 'Suggested thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work; Fixed-Game Reliability Question; Coalition Sampling and Budget Allocation; Metrics, References, and Uncertainty; Empirical Comparisons; Scope and Limitations; Conclusion. Organize results by agreement versus fidelity, allocation, and estimator/cost comparison, not task chronology. One shared thesis has condition-specific exact/approximate-reference evidence blocks.', 'The actual selected ICLR style has a 5.5-inch (about 397.5-point) text width and 9-inch text height. It is single-column: column-width and full-text-width coincide. All required figures use preferred_span=full_width and width fraction 1.0 of text width, not paper width or a fictitious two-column 0.48 span. Preserve anonymity and the supplied style; do not switch to the task scaffold NeurIPS template or assert the historical header alone verifies official-current-template provenance.', 'Use at most one generate-concept-figure diagram, editable and deterministic, without embedding invented measurements. Quantitative figures must have reproducible plotting sources and both PDF and PNG exports at 300 DPI. LaTeX references PDF whenever available. A raster-only full-width fallback must be regenerated at least 2400 pixels wide; column-only fallback at least 1200 pixels wide. Never upscale an existing raster. Keep final labels at least 8.5 points (9 for the overview), and simplify/split rather than shrink dense panels.', 'Only cite existing, actually consulted, safely screened references. Exact starter matches presently include Lundberg2017AUA and Musco2024ProvablyAS. The bibliography also contains broad-query noise; inclusion in it does not authorize access, citation, or novelty claims. Do not inspect unapproved surveys, citation chains, related-paper lists, or the prohibited prior study; no external retrieval was performed in this framing stage. Describe an empirical audit contribution without claiming priority or exhaustive literature coverage.', 'Do not create component-isolation ablations, estimator tournaments, architectural transfers, causal diagnoses of the negative allocation result, new datasets, or reliability certificates. The search-only conditioning and alias variants are unnecessary narrative baggage; substantive available protocol and retained rank/sign/cost details belong after references. A later authoritative analysis ranking may add appendix analyses without retroactively changing this strategy.', 'Reader-facing prose may describe the frozen configuration, original comparator, final measured audit, and evaluator-reported completion requirements. Internal field names in this JSON and source identifiers are private-only provenance, not visible manuscript terminology. Publication readiness is not scientific qualification, and scientific qualification is not high-risk deployment approval.']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
