     0.055768108795392,\n     -0.014866427591239531,\n     -0.0474088329268778,\n     0.03380390842753227,\n     0.0019179182996714862,\n     -0.04761935578793507,\n     -0.007599532698335339,\n     -0.01292421027657508,\n     -0.011276393061806373,\n     -0.026541330665878445,\n     -0.001492811081212591,\n     -0.02459533035146869,\n     0.0024016873170170563,\n     0.010092993154679682,\n     -0.009621085126456572,\n     0.02249274042486626,\n     0.0007761344891689947\n    ],\n    [\n     -0.07816585002784676,\n     0.007976265532806568,\n     -0.023807455396346416,\n     0.049145115082145766,\n     -0.009342154285138203,\n     -0.03729368438402593,\n     0.02540255668862072,\n     0.015084406208047086\nfocus [\n \"Primary: show repeat top-three-set overlap and reference-fidelity quality separately by dataset, model family, and fitted seed, using existing within-fit input-cluster intervals. Their scales have different meanings; never subtract them or interpret overlap as a probability of a correct explanation.\",\n \"Primary: report the observed averaging-minus-one-long-run quality difference, with its signed zero reference and stored within-fit intervals. The final mean is -0.03883354541895445; it is not a candidate-minus-original-baseline improvement.\",\n \"Direct descriptive comparison: frozen sampler versus library Kernel SHAP reference fidelity at nominal budgets 64 and 256, separating both fits and datasets. Check actual prediction rows and distinguish wall durations from package CPU counters.\",\n \"Condition specificity: distinguish the exact ACSIncome reference setting from approximate German Credit references. Dataset differences are confounded with dimension, data composition, reference construction, and fitted models, not an isolated mechanism.\",\n \"Report numerical efficiency residuals and evaluator-reported control/completion outcomes as checks, not attribution accuracy, causal validity, or high-risk deployment certification.\",\n \"Keep search selection and final findings separate. Use study.* for attempt counts and score differences; never turn missing attempts into losses. Omit conditioning/alias branches from core results because there are no controlled final component ablations.\"\n]\nfig ids [('fixed_game_overview', 'At most six semantic groups: fixed model/input/background and probability estimand; coalition sampling; repeated attributions and library comparator; agreement and fidelity readouts; exact ACSIncome/two approximate German references; four short versus one long allocation. Mark evidence scope and unverified diagnostics in the caption. Arrows denote data dependencies, not discovery order or a production certification pipeline.'), ('agreement_and_reference_fidelity', 'Rows: German Credit/ACSIncome; columns: repeat overlap/reference fidelity. Show two fits individually. Use case means and stored input_cluster_intervals, both pooled over the same background/budget levels. Caption labels intervals descriptive within-fit 95% input-cluster bootstrap intervals; do not attach pooled intervals to budget-specific points. Explain that exact and approximate fidelity anchors differ.'), ('budget_allocation_contrast', 'Show both fitted seeds separately with stored gain intervals and one common signed interpretation. German gain uses the mean reference vector, whereas its ordinary fidelity metric averages qualities to each reference. Equal coalition count also yields equal candidate oracle masked-row count for a fixed background; it does not imply equal runtime. No significance stars or universal loss claim.'), ('deployment_estimator_comparison', 'Four series: studied-64, studied-256, library-64, library-256. Average within retained input/background cells and candidate repeats, preserving the two fitted seeds in separate panels. Package calls have no estimated seed-to-seed variance. Reconstruct only deterministic summaries from stored vectors, verify candidate reductions against existing summaries, and record formulas and sources. Plot no fabricated error bars. Do not identify the library implementation with the original independent sampler; nominal coalition budgets need not imply identical prediction-row costs.')]\nsupp {'purpose': 'Provide substantive estimand, implementation, uncertainty, provenance, and reproduction detail after references without moving the negative allocation finding, reference limitations, or evidence-trust caveat out of the main paper.', 'planned_subsections': [{'heading': 'Fixed empirical games and implementation details', 'grounded_content': 'Document original-column players, probability-scale interventional masking, train-fitted preprocessing, kernel-size law, complement-pair coverage and rank-headroom formula, and identical constrained solver. Include source listings/precise pseudocode from staged implementations and the documented interface limits, not an invented package implementation equivalence. Pairing rank headroom is not a full-rank or accuracy guarantee.', 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes']}, {'heading': 'Data, fitted models, and reproduction manifest', 'grounded_content': 'Expand measured training/validation/selection row counts, validation accuracies, model hashes, final seeds, costs, and exact-reference counters from retained case records. Cross-reference task/evaluate_final.py, task/requirements.txt, and task/resources/final/manifest.json for public source versions, split rules, CPU environment, package versions, and exact model hyperparameters; these files are protocol evidence, not additional measured results. Preserve protected held-out-example restrictions and anonymous submission conventions.', 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes']}, {'heading': 'Metric definitions and descriptive uncertainty', 'grounded_content': 'Give the exact normalized L1 quality, top-three overlap/tie handling, rank and sign agreement definitions, efficiency residual, German fidelity-versus-gain reference distinction, equal-level aggregation, and existing 200-draw input-cluster intervals. Explain conditioning on each of two fits and the dependence of repeat pairs/backgrounds. Include retained budget/background-resolved tables and rank/sign summaries only as deterministic reconstructions from stored vectors, not new experiments.', 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.repeat_agreement', 'final.metric.reference_fidelity', 'final.metric.reference_resolution_quality', 'final.metric.local_accuracy_quality', 'final.metric.matched_budget_gain']}, {'heading': 'Reference sensitivity and measured computational work', 'grounded_content': 'Report both high-budget reference vectors and their disagreement, exact ACSIncome counters, library actual prediction rows and CPU seconds, and candidate observed wall durations/oracle masked-row totals. Show budget/background splits without conflating distinct empirical games; no reference convergence certificate, universal runtime benefit, or counterfactual CPU-hour measurement.', 'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes', 'final.metric.reference_resolution_quality']}, {'heading': 'Selection provenance and evaluation scope', 'grounded_content': 'State frozen non-winner selection, original comparator search score and zero score difference, three scored and zero unscored attempts, independently completed/qualified final evaluation, unverified retained diagnostics, tree-digest/linkage limitations, and missing gate-level detail. Explain that search score was an evaluator-defined completion/control proxy rather than a reliability objective; keep its internal field names out of reader-facing prose. Retain controls/replay evidence as checks and exclude replay from scientific aggregates.', 'source_ids': ['study.selection_kind', 'study.investigation_outcome', 'study.attempts.total', 'study.attempts.scored', 'study.attempts.unscored', 'study.baseline_score', 'study.search_score', 'study.search_score_delta', 'final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct', 'final.metric.control_pass_fraction', 'final.metric.coverage', 'final.evidence.episodes']}, {'heading': 'LLM Usage', 'grounded_content': 'Disclose the documented use of LLM assistance for research ideation, code preparation, reference planning, and framing/writing assistance. Distinguish candidate implementation from evaluator-owned observations, and do not invent human supervision, independent audits, or tools not documented. This section may follow the technical supplement under VENUE.md.', 'source_ids': ['study.selection_kind', 'final.evidence.episodes']}]}\ntotal 124\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 17:08 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root  root    180 Nov 17 17:23 ..\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    41 Nov 17 16:25 .agentic_resume_policy.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  1656 Nov 17 17:00 .downstream_selection.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   166 Nov 17 17:00 .investigation_completion.json\n-rw------- 2 agent agent   138 Nov 17 16:25 .task.agentic_task_ready.67725d2ced13be4973a74353c28aa197b9a5c6f209d65e8c6f1e5f48e689be8d\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 17:00 downstream\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 17:07 final_evaluation\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 16:40 investigation\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 17:23 metrics\ndrwx------ 7 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 17:24 paper\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 72477 Nov 17 17:24 pipeline_events.jsonl\ndrwxrwxr-x 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 16:25 task\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 16:25 task_drafting\n../investigation/conclusions.md\n../investigation/idea_generation_failures.jsonl\n../investigation/attempts_history.jsonl\n../investigation/events.jsonl\n../investigation/_idea_generation/cycle_0003_attempt_01_1794933898186547678/idea_agent_codex_20261117_164458.log\n../investigation/_idea_generation/cycle_0003_attempt_01_1794933898186547678/target_rubrics.json\n../investigation/_idea_generation/cycle_0003_attempt_01_1794933898186547678/idea_prompt.md\n../investigation/_ide