{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Larger values indicate less normalized error; this is a transformation, not a calibrated probability or an application acceptability threshold. Small reference norms can amplify normalized error.\n+Larger values indicate less normalized error; this is a transformation, not a calibrated probability or an application acceptability threshold. Small reference norms can amplify normalized error.\n@@\n-The allocation contrast is\n+The distinction between these diagnostics is structural. Adding a zero-sum perturbation to an attribution vector preserves efficiency while potentially changing every coordinate. Likewise, perturbations that preserve the leading absolute-feature set leave top-feature overlap unchanged even when attribution magnitudes differ. These observations explain why an efficiency check or repeated feature selection cannot replace Equation~\\\\ref{eq:quality}. They are consequences of the metric definitions, not additional measured controls. Reference fidelity still requires a defensible target: a vector can be close to an empirical-game reference without describing conditional dependence or a causal intervention in the underlying population.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L785]]\n+\n+The allocation contrast is\n@@\n-\\\\paragraph{Reference quality and statistical scope.}\n+\\\\paragraph{Nonlinear summaries require care.}\n+The bounded quality transformation compresses large discrepancies, and its average cannot be inverted to recover an average normalized error. In particular, the complement of mean quality is not a measured attribution-error fraction. Pooling across backgrounds and budgets also averages different finite games and computational conditions. A deployment decision would need the distribution relevant to its own fixed game and tolerance, not only the balanced aggregate used here. Our pooled readouts are useful for describing the retained grid, while the separated fits and budget-specific comparisons preserve distinctions that the aggregate hides. They do not identify which new input will be well explained.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L785]]\n+% @evidence[[derived_summary.json#/cases]]\n+\n+\\\\paragraph{Reference quality and statistical scope.}\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython scripts/build_claims.py\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\npython .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\npdflatex -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex > /tmp/latex-expanded.log 2>&1; tail -4 /tmp/latex-expanded.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
